{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbABpaWrbTfBCsrGGqs1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AwwGUax26TFQPxmdnxhoAG","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/agent/task-workspaces/030540ef-d69a-4c2c-839d-f4970e8c94d7/docs/specs/task-drafts.spec.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1331,"cache_read_input_tokens":25753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1331},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1377bc6f-2d4f-4260-bb35-736fcc1821d0","uuid":"2cc7bcd7-4e0b-429c-b0e8-1f015298cd42","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:10:34.909Z","request_id":"req_011CgbABpLsh9TVpzAXDRsTK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AwwGUax26TFQPxmdnxhoAG":{"file_path":"/workspace/agent/task-workspaces/030540ef-d69a-4c2c-839d-f4970e8c94d7/docs/specs/task-drafts.spec.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AwwGUax26TFQPxmdnxhoAG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Task drafts\n2\t\n3\t# 1. Purpose and Scope\n4\t\n5\t`create_task` makes a task claimable in the transaction that creates it. An\n6\toperator or orchestrator assembling several related tasks therefore races the\n7\tfleet: a task can be claimed before its dependencies, pins or acceptance\n8\tcriteria are added by a later `edit_task`/`set_task_dependencies`, and once\n9\tit is claimed most of its definition is immutable ([task edit](task-edit.spec.md)\n10\t3.4). Creating dependents first is impossible, because a dependency must exist.\n11\t\n12\tThis spec adds **task drafts**: persisted, editable task definitions that are not\n13\ttasks. A draft is never listed, counted, claimable or eligible; it becomes a task\n14\tonly through an explicit **publish**, which validates the whole batch and creates\n15\tevery task with its complete definition and real dependency edges in one write\n16\ttransaction.\n17\t\n18\tSurfaces, all calling one module, `tasks.drafts`:\n19\t\n20\t- REST under `/api/task-drafts` (3.6);\n21\t- MCP `create_task_draft`, `list_task_drafts`, `get_task_draft`,\n22\t  `edit_task_draft`, `discard_task_draft`, `publish_task_drafts`, thin calls to\n23\t  REST like every other tool ([MCP operations](mcp-operations.spec.md) 3.4).\n24\t\n25\t`POST /api/tasks` and MCP `create_task` are unchanged and stay the direct path.\n26\t\n27\t# 2. Non-Goals\n28\t\n29\t- No change to `create_task`, `edit_task` or the dependency rules of existing\n30\t  tasks; no new required field for tasks in general (no repository or coding\n31\t  fields): a non-coding task drafts and publishes like any other.\n32\t- No arbitrary cancellation, provider pins policy or deployment changes.\n33\t- No dashboard editor in this spec; drafts are a REST/MCP surface first.\n34\t- No per-project or per-author permissions (none exist,\n35\t  [knowledge](knowledge.spec.md) 3.1): every manager sees every draft.\n36\t- No \"unpublish\": a published task is a task, changed with `edit_task` or cancelled.\n37\t\n38\t# 3. Decisions Made\n39\t\n40\t## 3.1 Draft\n41\t\n42\tA draft is a row of `task_drafts` (migration `0065_task_drafts`):\n43\t`id`, `body` (JSON), `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_by`, `updated_at`,\n44\tand, once published, `published_at`, `published_task_id`, `publication_key`.\n45\t\n46\t- `body` takes every `TaskCreate` field, with the same per-field rules (lengths,\n47\t  ranges, enums, providers), plus `depends_on_drafts`: ids of other drafts. Saving\n48\t  is lenient about *completeness* only: `title` may be empty and `spec`,\n49\t  `acceptance` and `project` missing until publish. Unknown keys are refused\n50\t  (`422 validation_failed`).\n51\t- `depends_on` holds ids of **existing tasks**; `depends_on_drafts` holds ids of\n52\t  **drafts**. They are separate fields, so an id is never guessed to be one or\n53\t  the other. Together they are at most 100 (task dependencies 3.1).\n54\t- `version` is the draft's `updated_at`. Every successful edit yields a new,\n55\t  strictly greater version.\n56\t- A draft is read back whole with `GET /api/task-drafts/{id}`. A published draft\n57\t  stays as the record of what was published and carries `published_task_id`.\n58\t- Drafts survive restarts: they are rows in the database like tasks.\n59\t- Drafts are never in `tasks`, so no claim, list, inbox, overview, metric,\n60\t  routine or reaper ever sees them. Workers cannot read them either (3.5).\n61\t\n62\t## 3.2 Lifecycle\n63\t\n64\t```\n65\tcreate ──▶ open ──edit (expected_version)──▶ open ──publish──▶ published\n66\t             └──discard (expected_version)──▶ (row deleted)\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\t- **Edit** (`PATCH`) takes `{expected_version, changes}`: a partial patch of\n70\t  `body` fields. A field left out is kept; `null` resets it to its default; a\n71\t  list is replaced whole. The merged body is checked with the save rules. A\n72\t  mismatched `expected_version` is `409 stale_version` with the current version\n73\t  in `details`; nothing changes. A patch that changes nothing writes nothing\n74\t  and keeps the version.\n75\t- **Discard** (`DELETE ?expected_version=`) removes an open draft. Version rules\n76\t  as for edit. Another open draft that still names it in `depends_on_drafts`\n77\t  then fails publish validation until it is edited.\n78\t- A published draft refuses edit and discard with `409 draft_published`.\n79\t- At most **200 open drafts** exist at once (`409 too_many_drafts`), so the\n80\t  list is always whole.\n81\t\n82\t## 3.3 Publish\n83\t\n84\t`POST /api/task-drafts/publish` with:\n85\t\n86\t```\n87\t{ \"idempotency_key\": \"…\", \"mode\": \"atomic\" | \"partial\",\n88\t  \"drafts\": [{\"draft_id\": \"…\", \"expected_version\": \"…\"}, …] }\n89\t```\n90\t\n91\t- 1–**50** drafts per call, each named once. `idempotency_key` is 1–200\n92\t  characters and required. `mode` defaults to `atomic`. **Both REST and MCP\n93\t  offer both modes**; MCP's `publish_task_drafts` takes the same `mode`\n94\t  argument with the same default.\n95\t- **Validation** of each draft, all inside the write transaction, before any\n96\t  task is written:\n97\t  - the draft exists (else `not_found`), is open (else `draft_published`) and is\n98\t    at `expected_version` (else `stale_version`);\n99\t  - the body is a valid `TaskCreate` (title 1–200 characters, …);\n100\t  - **completeness**: a non-blank `spec` and at least one acceptance criterion,\n101\t    none blank (`validation_failed`). Only drafts require this; direct create\n102\t    does not;\n103\t  - the kind exists and its input schema holds; the project exists (a draft\n104\t    without `parent_id` must name one, `project_required`); pinned pages exist;\n105\t    the harness account pin resolves (the create rules, `check_create`);\n106\t  - **capabilities**: every required capability (after the kind's defaults) is\n107\t    declared by at least one pool or one non-archived agent\n108\t    (`unknown_capability`); a capability nobody can serve would leave the task\n109\t    `ready` forever;\n110\t  - **dependencies**: every `depends_on` task exists (`not_found`); every\n111\t    `depends_on_drafts` id is in this batch or names a draft that is already\n112\t    published (then its `published_task_id` is used). Anything else is\n113\t    `validation_failed` (`depends_on_drafts: <id> is not in this batch`).\n114\t    Edges among the batch must form no cycle, a self reference included\n115\t    (`dependency_cycle`, the path in `details`). New tasks have no dependents,\n116\t    so no cycle can pass through an existing task;\n117\t  - the caller's limits: the same per-agent hourly policy as `create_task`\n118\t    ([worker lifecycle](worker-lifecycle.spec.md) 3.10) applies to each task\n119\t    created; past it, the task waits in `awaiting_approval` with a `policy`\n120\t    decision instead of being refused.\n121\t- **Creation** runs in topological order of the batch's edges, through the same\n122\t  `tasks.service.create_task` as direct create: in-batch references are rewritten\n123\t  to the real new task ids, so each new task's dependencies exist and its state\n124\t  follows the usual rule (`ready` with no unfinished dependency, else `pending`;\n125\t  `awaiting_approval` with `requires_approval`). The draft is marked published\n126\t  with its task id and records `task_draft.published`. The tasks carry the\n127\t  ordinary `task.created` events.\n128\t- **Atomic** (`mode: atomic`): if any draft fails, nothing is written and the\n129\t  call fails with one error: `404 not_found` if a draft is missing, else\n130\t  `409 stale_version` if one is stale, else `409 draft_published`, else\n131\t  `422 dependency_cycle`, else `422 validation_failed`. `details` gives each\n132\t  failing item as `<draft_id>: <reason>`, so the outcome per item is explicit.\n133\t- **Partial** (`mode: partial`): every draft that passes is published, the\n134\t  others are not. A draft whose in-batch dependency was not published is not\n135\t  published either (`skipped`). The call answers `200` with an outcome per\n136\t  item.\n137\t- The answer (both modes, on success) is\n138\t  `{idempotency_key, mode, replayed, items: [{draft_id, outcome, task_id, state,\n139\t  code, errors}]}` in request order, `outcome` one of `published`, `rejected`\n140\t  (with `code` and `errors`) or `skipped` (with `errors` naming the draft it\n141\t  waited on).\n142\t\n143\t## 3.4 Idempotency, retries and concurrency\n144\t\n145\t- A successful publish stores `{key, request digest, answer}` in\n146\t  `task_draft_publications` in the same transaction. Repeating the same key with\n147\t  the same request (same mode, ids and versions) returns the stored answer with\n148\t  `replayed: true` and writes nothing: no duplicate task, even when the first\n149\t  answer was lost. The same key with another request is\n150\t  `409 idempotency_key_reused`.\n151\t- A refused atomic publish stores nothing (nothing happened); a retry with the\n152\t  same key is evaluated again.\n153\t- Publishing a draft that another call already published is `draft_published`\n154\t  for that item: a draft becomes at most one task, whatever the keys.\n155\t- **Publish versus claim.** Writes are serialized by the single writer\n156\t  ([single node](single-node.spec.md)). Tasks, edges, pins and the draft marks are\n157\t  inserted in one transaction, and readers see only committed data, so a claim\n158\t  sees either none of the batch or all of it with its complete definition and\n159\t  dependencies. A dependent can never be claimed before its in-batch\n160\t  dependency's edge exists.\n161\t- **Edit versus publish.** Publish checks each draft's `expected_version` inside\n162\t  the transaction: an edit that commits first makes the publish stale; a publish\n163\t  that commits first makes the edit `409 draft_published`.\n164\t\n165\t## 3.5 Permissions\n166\t\n167\tEvery draft endpoint and tool is orchestrator or admin only; workers get\n168\t`403 forbidden` on REST and the tools are not listed to them. A draft may hold an\n169\tunreviewed spec, so reads are restricted too. `403` is decided before the draft\n170\tis looked up. Actors are recorded as `admin:<label>` or `agent:<id>`.\n171\t\n172\t## 3.6 Interfaces and errors\n173\t\n174\t| REST | MCP | Notes |\n175\t| --- | --- | --- |\n176\t| `POST /api/task-drafts` (body fields) | `create_task_draft` | `201`, the draft |\n177\t| `GET /api/task-drafts` | `list_task_drafts` | open drafts, oldest first, `{items, total}` (whole: ≤ 200) |\n178\t| `GET /api/task-drafts/{id}` | `get_task_draft` | open or published |\n179\t| `PATCH /api/task-drafts/{id}` | `edit_task_draft` | 3.2 |\n180\t| `DELETE /api/task-drafts/{id}?expected_version=` | `discard_task_draft` | `204` |\n181\t| `POST /api/task-drafts/publish` | `publish_task_drafts` | 3.3; `atomic` or `partial` |\n182\t\n183\tErrors keep the shape `{detail: {code, message, details}}` on REST and\n184\t`<status> <code>: <message> | <details>` on MCP.\n185\t\n186\t| Status | `code` | When |\n187\t| --- | --- | --- |\n188\t| 403 | `forbidden` | not an orchestrator/admin token |\n189\t| 404 | `not_found` | draft (or, atomic, a dependency) does not exist |\n190\t| 409 | `stale_version` | `expected_version` is not current |\n191\t| 409 | `draft_published` | the draft was already published |\n192\t| 409 | `too_many_drafts` | 200 open drafts exist |\n193\t| 409 | `idempotency_key_reused` | the key was used for another request |\n194\t| 422 | `validation_failed` | a value breaks a rule; `details` per field or item |\n195\t| 422 | `dependency_cycle` | the batch's edges close a cycle |\n196\t\n197\t# 4. Open Questions\n198\t\n199\t- A dashboard draft editor, once operators ask for it.\n200\t- Whether old published drafts should be pruned; they are small and kept as the\n201\t  record for now.\n202\t\n203\t# 5. Constraints\n204\t\n205\t- One write transaction per operation, `tx.now` for time, no network call in it.\n206\t- One domain module for REST and MCP; MCP holds no rules (worker lifecycle 3.7).\n207\t- The schema change is additive (`task_drafts`, `task_draft_publications`) and\n208\t  written with `IF NOT EXISTS`, so it is idempotent.\n209\t- No secrets in events: `task_draft.published` carries ids only.\n210\t\n211\t# 6. Implementation Consequences\n212\t\n213\t1. This spec, its index link, and pointers in worker lifecycle (3.2, 3.6, 3.7),\n214\t   task edit, task dependencies and MCP operations.\n215\t2. Migration `0065_task_drafts.sql`; `argus_core.task_drafts` (body, patch and\n216\t   publish models); `argus_api.tasks.drafts` and its routes.\n217\t3. The six MCP tools and the orchestrator skill.\n218\t4. OpenAPI and the TypeScript client regenerated.\n219\t5. Tests in `apps/api/tests/test_task_drafts.py`.\n220\t\n221\t## Verification boundary\n222\t\n223\t- Commands: `make check`; `uv run pytest apps/api/tests/test_task_drafts.py`.\n224\t- Verified (unit and in-process API/MCP): nothing is claimable before publish;\n225\t  idempotent retries; dependency ids and edges; cycles; invalid payloads; publish\n226\t  against concurrent claims; persistence across reopen; stale edits;\n227\t  permissions; the migration upgrade from 0064 and its idempotence.\n228\t- Not verified: behaviour on a production database under real fleet load.\n229\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1377bc6f-2d4f-4260-bb35-736fcc1821d0","uuid":"6f142d9a-6051-4c5d-a792-8498dd6cf89f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:10:34.925Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/task-workspaces/030540ef-d69a-4c2c-839d-f4970e8c94d7/docs/specs/task-drafts.spec.md","content":"# Task drafts\n\n# 1. Purpose and Scope\n\n`create_task` makes a task claimable in the transaction that creates it. An\noperator or orchestrator assembling several related tasks therefore races the\nfleet: a task can be claimed before its dependencies, pins or acceptance\ncriteria are added by a later `edit_task`/`set_task_dependencies`, and once\nit is claimed most of its definition is immutable ([task edit](task-edit.spec.md)\n3.4). Creating dependents first is impossible, because a dependency must exist.\n\nThis spec adds **task drafts**: persisted, editable task definitions that are not\ntasks. A draft is never listed, counted, claimable or eligible; it becomes a task\nonly through an explicit **publish**, which validates the whole batch and creates\nevery task with its complete definition and real dependency edges in one write\ntransaction.\n\nSurfaces, all calling one module, `tasks.drafts`:\n\n- REST under `/api/task-drafts` (3.6);\n- MCP `create_task_draft`, `list_task_drafts`, `get_task_draft`,\n  `edit_task_draft`, `discard_task_draft`, `publish_task_drafts`, thin calls to\n  REST like every other tool ([MCP operations](mcp-operations.spec.md) 3.4).\n\n`POST /api/tasks` and MCP `create_task` are unchanged and stay the direct path.\n\n# 2. Non-Goals\n\n- No change to `create_task`, `edit_task` or the dependency rules of existing\n  tasks; no new required field for tasks in general (no repository or coding\n  fields): a non-coding task drafts and publishes like any other.\n- No arbitrary cancellation, provider pins policy or deployment changes.\n- No dashboard editor in this spec; drafts are a REST/MCP surface first.\n- No per-project or per-author permissions (none exist,\n  [knowledge](knowledge.spec.md) 3.1): every manager sees every draft.\n- No \"unpublish\": a published task is a task, changed with `edit_task` or cancelled.\n\n# 3. Decisions Made\n\n## 3.1 Draft\n\nA draft is a row of `task_drafts` (migration `0065_task_drafts`):\n`id`, `body` (JSON), `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_by`, `updated_at`,\nand, once published, `published_at`, `published_task_id`, `publication_key`.\n\n- `body` takes every `TaskCreate` field, with the same per-field rules (lengths,\n  ranges, enums, providers), plus `depends_on_drafts`: ids of other drafts. Saving\n  is lenient about *completeness* only: `title` may be empty and `spec`,\n  `acceptance` and `project` missing until publish. Unknown keys are refused\n  (`422 validation_failed`).\n- `depends_on` holds ids of **existing tasks**; `depends_on_drafts` holds ids of\n  **drafts**. They are separate fields, so an id is never guessed to be one or\n  the other. Together they are at most 100 (task dependencies 3.1).\n- `version` is the draft's `updated_at`. Every successful edit yields a new,\n  strictly greater version.\n- A draft is read back whole with `GET /api/task-drafts/{id}`. A published draft\n  stays as the record of what was published and carries `published_task_id`.\n- Drafts survive restarts: they are rows in the database like tasks.\n- Drafts are never in `tasks`, so no claim, list, inbox, overview, metric,\n  routine or reaper ever sees them. Workers cannot read them either (3.5).\n\n## 3.2 Lifecycle\n\n```\ncreate ──▶ open ──edit (expected_version)──▶ open ──publish──▶ published\n             └──discard (expected_version)──▶ (row deleted)\n```\n\n- **Edit** (`PATCH`) takes `{expected_version, changes}`: a partial patch of\n  `body` fields. A field left out is kept; `null` resets it to its default; a\n  list is replaced whole. The merged body is checked with the save rules. A\n  mismatched `expected_version` is `409 stale_version` with the current version\n  in `details`; nothing changes. A patch that changes nothing writes nothing\n  and keeps the version.\n- **Discard** (`DELETE ?expected_version=`) removes an open draft. Version rules\n  as for edit. Another open draft that still names it in `depends_on_drafts`\n  then fails publish validation until it is edited.\n- A published draft refuses edit and discard with `409 draft_published`.\n- At most **200 open drafts** exist at once (`409 too_many_drafts`), so the\n  list is always whole.\n\n## 3.3 Publish\n\n`POST /api/task-drafts/publish` with:\n\n```\n{ \"idempotency_key\": \"…\", \"mode\": \"atomic\" | \"partial\",\n  \"drafts\": [{\"draft_id\": \"…\", \"expected_version\": \"…\"}, …] }\n```\n\n- 1–**50** drafts per call, each named once. `idempotency_key` is 1–200\n  characters and required. `mode` defaults to `atomic`. **Both REST and MCP\n  offer both modes**; MCP's `publish_task_drafts` takes the same `mode`\n  argument with the same default.\n- **Validation** of each draft, all inside the write transaction, before any\n  task is written:\n  - the draft exists (else `not_found`), is open (else `draft_published`) and is\n    at `expected_version` (else `stale_version`);\n  - the body is a valid `TaskCreate` (title 1–200 characters, …);\n  - **completeness**: a non-blank `spec` and at least one acceptance criterion,\n    none blank (`validation_failed`). Only drafts require this; direct create\n    does not;\n  - the kind exists and its input schema holds; the project exists (a draft\n    without `parent_id` must name one, `project_required`); pinned pages exist;\n    the harness account pin resolves (the create rules, `check_create`);\n  - **capabilities**: every required capability (after the kind's defaults) is\n    declared by at least one pool or one non-archived agent\n    (`unknown_capability`); a capability nobody can serve would leave the task\n    `ready` forever;\n  - **dependencies**: every `depends_on` task exists (`not_found`); every\n    `depends_on_drafts` id is in this batch or names a draft that is already\n    published (then its `published_task_id` is used). Anything else is\n    `validation_failed` (`depends_on_drafts: <id> is not in this batch`).\n    Edges among the batch must form no cycle, a self reference included\n    (`dependency_cycle`, the path in `details`). New tasks have no dependents,\n    so no cycle can pass through an existing task;\n  - the caller's limits: the same per-agent hourly policy as `create_task`\n    ([worker lifecycle](worker-lifecycle.spec.md) 3.10) applies to each task\n    created; past it, the task waits in `awaiting_approval` with a `policy`\n    decision instead of being refused.\n- **Creation** runs in topological order of the batch's edges, through the same\n  `tasks.service.create_task` as direct create: in-batch references are rewritten\n  to the real new task ids, so each new task's dependencies exist and its state\n  follows the usual rule (`ready` with no unfinished dependency, else `pending`;\n  `awaiting_approval` with `requires_approval`). The draft is marked published\n  with its task id and records `task_draft.published`. The tasks carry the\n  ordinary `task.created` events.\n- **Atomic** (`mode: atomic`): if any draft fails, nothing is written and the\n  call fails with one error: `404 not_found` if a draft is missing, else\n  `409 stale_version` if one is stale, else `409 draft_published`, else\n  `422 dependency_cycle`, else `422 validation_failed`. `details` gives each\n  failing item as `<draft_id>: <reason>`, so the outcome per item is explicit.\n- **Partial** (`mode: partial`): every draft that passes is published, the\n  others are not. A draft whose in-batch dependency was not published is not\n  published either (`skipped`). The call answers `200` with an outcome per\n  item.\n- The answer (both modes, on success) is\n  `{idempotency_key, mode, replayed, items: [{draft_id, outcome, task_id, state,\n  code, errors}]}` in request order, `outcome` one of `published`, `rejected`\n  (with `code` and `errors`) or `skipped` (with `errors` naming the draft it\n  waited on).\n\n## 3.4 Idempotency, retries and concurrency\n\n- A successful publish stores `{key, request digest, answer}` in\n  `task_draft_publications` in the same transaction. Repeating the same key with\n  the same request (same mode, ids and versions) returns the stored answer with\n  `replayed: true` and writes nothing: no duplicate task, even when the first\n  answer was lost. The same key with another request is\n  `409 idempotency_key_reused`.\n- A refused atomic publish stores nothing (nothing happened); a retry with the\n  same key is evaluated again.\n- Publishing a draft that another call already published is `draft_published`\n  for that item: a draft becomes at most one task, whatever the keys.\n- **Publish versus claim.** Writes are serialized by the single writer\n  ([single node](single-node.spec.md)). Tasks, edges, pins and the draft marks are\n  inserted in one transaction, and readers see only committed data, so a claim\n  sees either none of the batch or all of it with its complete definition and\n  dependencies. A dependent can never be claimed before its in-batch\n  dependency's edge exists.\n- **Edit versus publish.** Publish checks each draft's `expected_version` inside\n  the transaction: an edit that commits first makes the publish stale; a publish\n  that commits first makes the edit `409 draft_published`.\n\n## 3.5 Permissions\n\nEvery draft endpoint and tool is orchestrator or admin only; workers get\n`403 forbidden` on REST and the tools are not listed to them. A draft may hold an\nunreviewed spec, so reads are restricted too. `403` is decided before the draft\nis looked up. Actors are recorded as `admin:<label>` or `agent:<id>`.\n\n## 3.6 Interfaces and errors\n\n| REST | MCP | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `POST /api/task-drafts` (body fields) | `create_task_draft` | `201`, the draft |\n| `GET /api/task-drafts` | `list_task_drafts` | open drafts, oldest first, `{items, total}` (whole: ≤ 200) |\n| `GET /api/task-drafts/{id}` | `get_task_draft` | open or published |\n| `PATCH /api/task-drafts/{id}` | `edit_task_draft` | 3.2 |\n| `DELETE /api/task-drafts/{id}?expected_version=` | `discard_task_draft` | `204` |\n| `POST /api/task-drafts/publish` | `publish_task_drafts` | 3.3; `atomic` or `partial` |\n\nErrors keep the shape `{detail: {code, message, details}}` on REST and\n`<status> <code>: <message> | <details>` on MCP.\n\n| Status | `code` | When |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 403 | `forbidden` | not an orchestrator/admin token |\n| 404 | `not_found` | draft (or, atomic, a dependency) does not exist |\n| 409 | `stale_version` | `expected_version` is not current |\n| 409 | `draft_published` | the draft was already published |\n| 409 | `too_many_drafts` | 200 open drafts exist |\n| 409 | `idempotency_key_reused` | the key was used for another request |\n| 422 | `validation_failed` | a value breaks a rule; `details` per field or item |\n| 422 | `dependency_cycle` | the batch's edges close a cycle |\n\n# 4. Open Questions\n\n- A dashboard draft editor, once operators ask for it.\n- Whether old published drafts should be pruned; they are small and kept as the\n  record for now.\n\n# 5. Constraints\n\n- One write transaction per operation, `tx.now` for time, no network call in it.\n- One domain module for REST and MCP; MCP holds no rules (worker lifecycle 3.7).\n- The schema change is additive (`task_drafts`, `task_draft_publications`) and\n  written with `IF NOT EXISTS`, so it is idempotent.\n- No secrets in events: `task_draft.published` carries ids only.\n\n# 6. Implementation Consequences\n\n1. This spec, its index link, and pointers in worker lifecycle (3.2, 3.6, 3.7),\n   task edit, task dependencies and MCP operations.\n2. Migration `0065_task_drafts.sql`; `argus_core.task_drafts` (body, patch and\n   publish models); `argus_api.tasks.drafts` and its routes.\n3. The six MCP tools and the orchestrator skill.\n4. OpenAPI and the TypeScript client regenerated.\n5. Tests in `apps/api/tests/test_task_drafts.py`.\n\n## Verification boundary\n\n- Commands: `make check`; `uv run pytest apps/api/tests/test_task_drafts.py`.\n- Verified (unit and in-process API/MCP): nothing is claimable before publish;\n  idempotent retries; dependency ids and edges; cycles; invalid payloads; publish\n  against concurrent claims; persistence across reopen; stale edits;\n  permissions; the migration upgrade from 0064 and its idempotence.\n- Not verified: behaviour on a production database under real fleet load.\n","numLines":229,"startLine":1,"totalLines":229}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AwwGUax26TFQPxmdnxhoAG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbABpaWrbTfBCsrGGqs1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Er9YseZpFfmp3eViB2qze","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/agent/task-workspaces/030540ef-d69a-4c2c-839d-f4970e8c94d7/apps/api/src/argus_api/tasks/drafts.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1331,"cache_read_input_tokens":25753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1331},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1377bc6f-2d4f-4260-bb35-736fcc1821d0","uuid":"1f28c733-eb4a-4803-b87e-0f6b17b0b1c0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:10:35.441Z","request_id":"req_011CgbABpLsh9TVpzAXDRsTK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015Er9YseZpFfmp3eViB2qze":{"file_path":"/workspace/agent/task-workspaces/030540ef-d69a-4c2c-839d-f4970e8c94d7/apps/api/src/argus_api/tasks/drafts.py"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Er9YseZpFfmp3eViB2qze","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Task drafts and their publication (docs/specs/task-drafts.spec.md).\n2\t\n3\tThe one implementation behind REST and MCP. A draft is a row of `task_drafts`,\n4\tnever of `tasks`, so nothing can claim it; publish creates every task of a batch\n5\tthrough `service.create_task` in the caller's single write transaction.\n6\t\"\"\"\n7\t\n8\timport hashlib\n9\timport json\n10\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n11\tfrom typing import Any\n12\tfrom uuid import uuid4\n13\t\n14\timport aiosqlite\n15\tfrom argus_core.task_drafts import (\n16\t    MAX_OPEN_DRAFTS,\n17\t    PublishOutcome,\n18\t    PublishRequest,\n19\t    PublishResult,\n20\t    TaskDraft,\n21\t    TaskDraftBody,\n22\t    TaskDraftPage,\n23\t)\n24\tfrom argus_core.tasks import TaskCreate\n25\tfrom pydantic import ValidationError\n26\t\n27\tfrom argus_api.db import Tx, ts\n28\tfrom argus_api.errors import (\n29\t    ConflictError,\n30\t    DomainError,\n31\t    NotFoundError,\n32\t    ValidationFailedError,\n33\t)\n34\tfrom argus_api.events import record\n35\tfrom argus_api.tasks import service\n36\t\n37\t_TICK = timedelta(microseconds=1)\n38\t# Which refusal an atomic publish reports when several items fail (3.3).\n39\t_PRECEDENCE = (\"not_found\", \"stale_version\", \"draft_published\", \"dependency_cycle\")\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t# -- reads -------------------------------------------------------------------\n43\t\n44\t\n45\tasync def get_draft(conn: aiosqlite.Connection, draft_id: str) -> TaskDraft:\n46\t    return _to_draft(await _row(conn, draft_id))\n47\t\n48\t\n49\tasync def list_drafts(conn: aiosqlite.Connection) -> TaskDraftPage:\n50\t    async with conn.execute(\n51\t        \"SELECT * FROM task_drafts WHERE published_at IS NULL ORDER BY created_at, id\"\n52\t    ) as cur:\n53\t        items = [_to_draft(r) for r in await cur.fetchall()]\n54\t    return TaskDraftPage(items=items, total=len(items))\n55\t\n56\t\n57\t# -- open drafts -------------------------------------------------------------\n58\t\n59\t\n60\tasync def create_draft(tx: Tx, body: TaskDraftBody, actor: str) -> TaskDraft:\n61\t    async with tx.conn.execute(\n62\t        \"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM task_drafts WHERE published_at IS NULL\"\n63\t    ) as cur:\n64\t        row = await cur.fetchone()\n65\t    if row is not None and row[0] >= MAX_OPEN_DRAFTS:\n66\t        raise ConflictError(\n67\t            f\"at most {MAX_OPEN_DRAFTS} open drafts; publish or discard some first\",\n68\t            code=\"too_many_drafts\",\n69\t        )\n70\t    draft_id = str(uuid4())\n71\t    now = ts(tx.now)\n72\t    await tx.conn.execute(\n73\t        \"INSERT INTO task_drafts (id, body, created_by, created_at, updated_by,\"\n74\t        \" updated_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n75\t        (draft_id, _stored(body), actor, now, actor, now),\n76\t    )\n77\t    return await get_draft(tx.conn, draft_id)\n78\t\n79\t\n80\tasync def edit_draft(\n81\t    tx: Tx, draft_id: str, changes: dict[str, Any], expected_version: str, actor: str\n82\t) -> TaskDraft:\n83\t    \"\"\"Merge a partial patch into an open draft's body: `null` resets a field.\"\"\"\n84\t    row = await _open_row(tx.conn, draft_id, expected_version)\n85\t    stored = json.loads(row[\"body\"])\n86\t    merged = {k: v for k, v in {**stored, **changes}.items() if v is not None}\n87\t    try:\n88\t        body = TaskDraftBody.model_validate(merged)\n89\t    except ValidationError as exc:\n90\t        raise ValidationFailedError(\n91\t            \"invalid draft: \" + \"; \".join(_errors(exc)), details=_errors(exc)\n92\t        ) from None\n93\t    if json.loads(_stored(body)) == stored:\n94\t        return _to_draft(row)  # nothing differs: no write, same version\n95\t    version = ts(max(tx.now, datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"updated_at\"]) + _TICK))\n96\t    await tx.conn.execute(\n97\t        \"UPDATE task_drafts SET body = ?, updated_by = ?, updated_at = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n98\t        (_stored(body), actor, version, draft_id),\n99\t    )\n100\t    return await get_draft(tx.conn, draft_id)\n101\t\n102\t\n103\tasync def discard_draft(tx: Tx, draft_id: str, expected_version: str) -> None:\n104\t    await _open_row(tx.conn, draft_id, expected_version)\n105\t    await tx.conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM task_drafts WHERE id = ?\", (draft_id,))\n106\t\n107\t\n108\t# -- publication -------------------------------------------------------------\n109\t\n110\t\n111\tasync def publish(\n112\t    tx: Tx, req: PublishRequest, actor: str, *, hourly_limit: int | None = None\n113\t) -> PublishResult:\n114\t    \"\"\"Validate and publish a batch (3.3), idempotently by key (3.4).\"\"\"\n115\t    digest = _digest(req)\n116\t    async with tx.conn.execute(\n117\t        \"SELECT request_digest, answer FROM task_draft_publications\"\n118\t        \" WHERE idempotency_key = ?\",\n119\t        (req.idempotency_key,),\n120\t    ) as cur:\n121\t        seen = await cur.fetchone()\n122\t    if seen is not None:\n123\t        if seen[\"request_digest\"] != digest:\n124\t            raise ConflictError(\n125\t                \"this idempotency_key was used for another publish request\",\n126\t                code=\"idempotency_key_reused\",\n127\t            )\n128\t        answer = PublishResult.model_validate_json(seen[\"answer\"])\n129\t        return answer.model_copy(update={\"replayed\": True})\n130\t\n131\t    ids = [d.draft_id for d in req.drafts]\n132\t    rows = await _rows(tx.conn, ids)\n133\t    outcomes: dict[str, PublishOutcome] = {}\n134\t    bodies: dict[str, TaskDraftBody] = {}\n135\t    outside: dict[str, str] = {}  # published drafts outside the batch -> task id\n136\t    for item in req.drafts:\n137\t        row = rows.get(item.draft_id)\n138\t        if row is None:\n139\t            outcomes[item.draft_id] = _rejected(\n140\t                item.draft_id, \"not_found\", \"draft not found\"\n141\t            )\n142\t        elif row[\"published_at\"] is not None:\n143\t            outcomes[item.draft_id] = _rejected(\n144\t                item.draft_id,\n145\t                \"draft_published\",\n146\t                f\"already published as task {row['published_task_id']}\",\n147\t            )\n148\t        elif row[\"updated_at\"] != item.expected_version:\n149\t            outcomes[item.draft_id] = _rejected(\n150\t                item.draft_id,\n151\t                \"stale_version\",\n152\t                f\"draft changed since you read it (version {row['updated_at']})\",\n153\t            )\n154\t        else:\n155\t            bodies[item.draft_id] = TaskDraftBody.model_validate_json(row[\"body\"])\n156\t    refs = {d for b in bodies.values() for d in b.depends_on_drafts} - set(ids)\n157\t    for ref, row in (await _rows(tx.conn, sorted(refs))).items():\n158\t        if row[\"published_task_id\"] is not None:\n159\t            outside[ref] = row[\"published_task_id\"]\n160\t    for draft_id, body in bodies.items():\n161\t        if why := _incomplete(body, outside, set(ids)):\n162\t            outcomes[draft_id] = _rejected(draft_id, \"validation_failed\", *why)\n163\t\n164\t    order, cycles = _order(ids, {i: b.depends_on_drafts for i, b in bodies.items()})\n165\t    for draft_id, path in cycles.items():\n166\t        outcomes.setdefault(\n167\t            draft_id,\n168\t            _rejected(\n169\t                draft_id,\n170\t                \"dependency_cycle\",\n171\t                \"these drafts depend on each other: \" + \" -> \".join(path),\n172\t            ),\n173\t        )\n174\t\n175\t    task_ids: dict[str, str] = dict(outside)\n176\t    for draft_id in order:\n177\t        if draft_id in outcomes:\n178\t            continue\n179\t        body = bodies[draft_id]\n180\t        if waits := [d for d in body.depends_on_drafts if d not in task_ids]:\n181\t            outcomes[draft_id] = PublishOutcome(\n182\t                draft_id=draft_id,\n183\t                outcome=\"skipped\",\n184\t                errors=[f\"depends_on_drafts: {d} was not published\" for d in waits],\n185\t            )\n186\t            continue\n187\t        create = TaskCreate.model_validate(\n188\t            {\n189\t                **body.model_dump(exclude_unset=True, exclude={\"depends_on_drafts\"}),\n190\t                \"depends_on\": [\n191\t                    *body.depends_on,\n192\t                    *(task_ids[d] for d in body.depends_on_drafts),\n193\t                ],\n194\t            }\n195\t        )\n196\t        try:\n197\t            async with tx.savepoint():\n198\t                task = await service.create_task(\n199\t                    tx, create, actor, hourly_limit=hourly_limit\n200\t                )\n201\t                await _check_capabilities(tx.conn, task.required_capabilities)\n202\t                await tx.conn.execute(\n203\t                    \"UPDATE task_drafts SET published_at = ?, published_task_id = ?,\"\n204\t                    \" publication_key = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n205\t                    (ts(tx.now), task.id, req.idempotency_key, draft_id),\n206\t                )\n207\t                await record(\n208\t                    tx,\n209\t                    actor,\n210\t                    \"task_draft\",\n211\t                    draft_id,\n212\t                    \"task_draft.published\",\n213\t                    {\"task_id\": task.id, \"idempotency_key\": req.idempotency_key},\n214\t                )\n215\t        except DomainError as exc:\n216\t            outcomes[draft_id] = _rejected(\n217\t                draft_id, exc.code, exc.message, *exc.details\n218\t            )\n219\t            continue\n220\t        task_ids[draft_id] = task.id\n221\t        outcomes[draft_id] = PublishOutcome(\n222\t            draft_id=draft_id, outcome=\"published\", task_id=task.id, state=task.state\n223\t        )\n224\t\n225\t    result = PublishResult(\n226\t        idempotency_key=req.idempotency_key,\n227\t        mode=req.mode,\n228\t        items=[outcomes[i] for i in ids],\n229\t    )\n230\t    failed = [o for o in result.items if o.outcome != \"published\"]\n231\t    if req.mode == \"atomic\" and failed:\n232\t        raise _atomic_refusal(failed)  # the write transaction rolls back\n233\t    await tx.conn.execute(\n234\t        \"INSERT INTO task_draft_publications (idempotency_key, request_digest,\"\n235\t        \" answer, actor, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n236\t        (req.idempotency_key, digest, result.model_dump_json(), actor, ts(tx.now)),\n237\t    )\n238\t    return result\n239\t\n240\t\n241\tdef _incomplete(\n242\t    body: TaskDraftBody, outside: dict[str, str], batch: set[str]\n243\t) -> list[str]:\n244\t    \"\"\"Why a draft is not a complete task definition yet (3.3), or nothing.\"\"\"\n245\t    try:\n246\t        TaskCreate.model_validate(\n247\t            body.model_dump(exclude_unset=True, exclude={\"depends_on_drafts\"})\n248\t        )\n249\t        errors = []\n250\t    except ValidationError as exc:\n251\t        errors = _errors(exc)\n252\t    if not body.spec.strip():\n253\t        errors.append(\"spec: a draft needs a spec to be published\")\n254\t    if not body.acceptance:\n255\t        errors.append(\"acceptance: a draft needs at least one criterion\")\n256\t    elif any(not a.strip() for a in body.acceptance):\n257\t        errors.append(\"acceptance: criteria cannot be blank\")\n258\t    errors += [\n259\t        f\"depends_on_drafts: {d} is not in this batch\"\n260\t        for d in body.depends_on_drafts\n261\t        if d not in batch and d not in outside\n262\t    ]\n263\t    return errors\n264\t\n265\t\n266\tdef _order(\n267\t    ids: list[str], edges: dict[str, list[str]]\n268\t) -> tuple[list[str], dict[str, list[str]]]:\n269\t    \"\"\"The batch in dependency order, and each draft on an in-batch cycle with\n270\t    that cycle's path. Edges to drafts outside the batch are ignored here.\"\"\"\n271\t    batch = set(ids)\n272\t    deps = {i: [d for d in edges.get(i, []) if d in batch] for i in ids}\n273\t    order: list[str] = []\n274\t    done: set[str] = set()\n275\t    while True:\n276\t        ready = [i for i in ids if i not in done and all(d in done for d in deps[i])]\n277\t        if not ready:\n278\t            break\n279\t        order += ready\n280\t        done.update(ready)\n281\t    cycles: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n282\t    for start in ids:\n283\t        if start not in done and (path := _cycle_from(start, deps)):\n284\t            cycles[start] = path\n285\t    # Drafts left behind a cycle come last; they are skipped as not published.\n286\t    return order + [i for i in ids if i not in done], cycles\n287\t\n288\t\n289\tdef _cycle_from(start: str, deps: dict[str, list[str]]) -> list[str] | None:\n290\t    \"\"\"A path start -> ... -> start along dependency edges, if one exists.\"\"\"\n291\t    stack: list[tuple[str, list[str]]] = [(start, [start])]\n292\t    seen: set[str] = set()\n293\t    while stack:\n294\t        node, path = stack.pop()\n295\t        for dep in deps[node]:\n296\t            if dep == start:\n297\t                return [*path, start]\n298\t            if dep not in seen:\n299\t                seen.add(dep)\n300\t                stack.append((dep, [*path, dep]))\n301\t    return None\n302\t\n303\t\n304\tasync def _check_capabilities(conn: aiosqlite.Connection, required: list[str]) -> None:\n305\t    \"\"\"Each capability must be declared by a pool or a non-archived agent.\"\"\"\n306\t    if not required:\n307\t        return\n308\t    async with conn.execute(\n309\t        \"SELECT j.value FROM pools, json_each(pools.capabilities) AS j\"\n310\t        \" UNION SELECT j.value FROM agents, json_each(agents.capabilities) AS j\"\n311\t        \" WHERE agents.archived_at IS NULL\"\n312\t    ) as cur:\n313\t        known = {r[0] for r in await cur.fetchall()}\n314\t    if unknown := [c for c in required if c not in known]:\n315\t        raise ValidationFailedError(\n316\t            \"no pool or agent declares these capabilities: \" + \", \".join(unknown),\n317\t            code=\"unknown_capability\",\n318\t            details=[f\"required_capabilities: {c}\" for c in unknown],\n319\t        )\n320\t\n321\t\n322\tdef _atomic_refusal(failed: list[PublishOutcome]) -> DomainError:\n323\t    codes = [o.code for o in failed if o.code]\n324\t    code = next((c for c in _PRECEDENCE if c in codes), codes[0] if codes else None)\n325\t    cls = {\n326\t        \"not_found\": NotFoundError,\n327\t        \"stale_version\": ConflictError,\n328\t        \"draft_published\": ConflictError,\n329\t    }.get(code or \"\", ValidationFailedError)\n330\t    details = [\n331\t        f\"{o.draft_id}: {o.code or o.outcome}: {e}\" for o in failed for e in o.errors\n332\t    ]\n333\t    return cls(\n334\t        f\"nothing was published: {len(failed)} draft(s) cannot be published\",\n335\t        code=code if code in _PRECEDENCE else \"validation_failed\",\n336\t        details=details,\n337\t    )\n338\t\n339\t\n340\tdef _rejected(draft_id: str, code: str, *errors: str) -> PublishOutcome:\n341\t    return PublishOutcome(\n342\t        draft_id=draft_id, outcome=\"rejected\", code=code, errors=list(errors)\n343\t    )\n344\t\n345\t\n346\tdef _digest(req: PublishRequest) -> str:\n347\t    canonical = json.dumps(\n348\t        {\n349\t            \"mode\": req.mode,\n350\t            \"drafts\": [[d.draft_id, d.expected_version] for d in req.drafts],\n351\t        },\n352\t        separators=(\",\", \":\"),\n353\t    )\n354\t    return hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode()).hexdigest()\n355\t\n356\t\n357\t# -- rows --------------------------------------------------------------------\n358\t\n359\t\n360\tdef _stored(body: TaskDraftBody) -> str:\n361\t    # Only fields the author set: a kind's defaults still apply at publish.\n362\t    return json.dumps(body.model_dump(mode=\"json\", exclude_unset=True), sort_keys=True)\n363\t\n364\t\n365\tdef _errors(exc: ValidationError) -> list[str]:\n366\t    return [\n367\t        f\"{'.'.join(map(str, e['loc'])) or 'body'}: {e['msg']}\" for e in exc.errors()\n368\t    ]\n369\t\n370\t\n371\tasync def _row(conn: aiosqlite.Connection, draft_id: str) -> aiosqlite.Row:\n372\t    async with conn.execute(\n373\t        \"SELECT * FROM task_drafts WHERE id = ?\", (draft_id,)\n374\t    ) as cur:\n375\t        row = await cur.fetchone()\n376\t    if row is None:\n377\t        raise NotFoundError(f\"draft not found: {draft_id}\")\n378\t    return row\n379\t\n380\t\n381\tasync def _rows(conn: aiosqlite.Connection, ids: list[str]) -> dict[str, aiosqlite.Row]:\n382\t    if not ids:\n383\t        return {}\n384\t    marks = \",\".join(\"?\" * len(ids))\n385\t    sql = f\"SELECT * FROM task_drafts WHERE id IN ({marks})\"  # noqa: S608\n386\t    async with conn.execute(sql, ids) as cur:\n387\t        return {r[\"id\"]: r for r in await cur.fetchall()}\n388\t\n389\t\n390\tasync def _open_row(\n391\t    conn: aiosqlite.Connection, draft_id: str, expected_version: str\n392\t) -> aiosqlite.Row:\n393\t    row = await _row(conn, draft_id)\n394\t    if row[\"published_at\"] is not None:\n395\t        raise ConflictError(\n396\t            f\"draft {draft_id} was published as task {row['published_task_id']};\"\n397\t            \" edit the task instead\",\n398\t            code=\"draft_published\",\n399\t            details=[row[\"published_task_id\"]],\n400\t        )\n401\t    if row[\"updated_at\"] != expected_version:\n402\t        raise ConflictError(\n403\t            f\"draft {draft_id} changed since you read it (version\"\n404\t            f\" {row['updated_at']}); read it again and reapply your change\",\n405\t            code=\"stale_version\",\n406\t            details=[row[\"updated_at\"]],\n407\t        )\n408\t    return row\n409\t\n410\t\n411\tdef _to_draft(row: aiosqlite.Row) -> TaskDraft:\n412\t    return TaskDraft(\n413\t        id=row[\"id\"],\n414\t        body=TaskDraftBody.model_validate_json(row[\"body\"]),\n415\t        version=row[\"updated_at\"],\n416\t        created_by=row[\"created_by\"],\n417\t        created_at=row[\"created_at\"],\n418\t        updated_by=row[\"updated_by\"],\n419\t        updated_at=row[\"updated_at\"],\n420\t        published_at=row[\"published_at\"],\n421\t        published_task_id=row[\"published_task_id\"],\n422\t    )\n423\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1377bc6f-2d4f-4260-bb35-736fcc1821d0","uuid":"84a6c167-0045-41b6-be2a-6d3a5f74758b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:10:35.450Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/task-workspaces/030540ef-d69a-4c2c-839d-f4970e8c94d7/apps/api/src/argus_api/tasks/drafts.py","content":"\"\"\"Task drafts and their publication (docs/specs/task-drafts.spec.md).\n\nThe one implementation behind REST and MCP. A draft is a row of `task_drafts`,\nnever of `tasks`, so nothing can claim it; publish creates every task of a batch\nthrough `service.create_task` in the caller's single write transaction.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\nimport aiosqlite\nfrom argus_core.task_drafts import (\n    MAX_OPEN_DRAFTS,\n    PublishOutcome,\n    PublishRequest,\n    PublishResult,\n    TaskDraft,\n    TaskDraftBody,\n    TaskDraftPage,\n)\nfrom argus_core.tasks import TaskCreate\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError\n\nfrom argus_api.db import Tx, ts\nfrom argus_api.errors import (\n    ConflictError,\n    DomainError,\n    NotFoundError,\n    ValidationFailedError,\n)\nfrom argus_api.events import record\nfrom argus_api.tasks import service\n\n_TICK = timedelta(microseconds=1)\n# Which refusal an atomic publish reports when several items fail (3.3).\n_PRECEDENCE = (\"not_found\", \"stale_version\", \"draft_published\", \"dependency_cycle\")\n\n\n# -- reads -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nasync def get_draft(conn: aiosqlite.Connection, draft_id: str) -> TaskDraft:\n    return _to_draft(await _row(conn, draft_id))\n\n\nasync def list_drafts(conn: aiosqlite.Connection) -> TaskDraftPage:\n    async with conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT * FROM task_drafts WHERE published_at IS NULL ORDER BY created_at, id\"\n    ) as cur:\n        items = [_to_draft(r) for r in await cur.fetchall()]\n    return TaskDraftPage(items=items, total=len(items))\n\n\n# -- open drafts -------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nasync def create_draft(tx: Tx, body: TaskDraftBody, actor: str) -> TaskDraft:\n    async with tx.conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM task_drafts WHERE published_at IS NULL\"\n    ) as cur:\n        row = await cur.fetchone()\n    if row is not None and row[0] >= MAX_OPEN_DRAFTS:\n        raise ConflictError(\n            f\"at most {MAX_OPEN_DRAFTS} open drafts; publish or discard some first\",\n            code=\"too_many_drafts\",\n        )\n    draft_id = str(uuid4())\n    now = ts(tx.now)\n    await tx.conn.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO task_drafts (id, body, created_by, created_at, updated_by,\"\n        \" updated_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n        (draft_id, _stored(body), actor, now, actor, now),\n    )\n    return await get_draft(tx.conn, draft_id)\n\n\nasync def edit_draft(\n    tx: Tx, draft_id: str, changes: dict[str, Any], expected_version: str, actor: str\n) -> TaskDraft:\n    \"\"\"Merge a partial patch into an open draft's body: `null` resets a field.\"\"\"\n    row = await _open_row(tx.conn, draft_id, expected_version)\n    stored = json.loads(row[\"body\"])\n    merged = {k: v for k, v in {**stored, **changes}.items() if v is not None}\n    try:\n        body = TaskDraftBody.model_validate(merged)\n    except ValidationError as exc:\n        raise ValidationFailedError(\n            \"invalid draft: \" + \"; \".join(_errors(exc)), details=_errors(exc)\n        ) from None\n    if json.loads(_stored(body)) == stored:\n        return _to_draft(row)  # nothing differs: no write, same version\n    version = ts(max(tx.now, datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"updated_at\"]) + _TICK))\n    await tx.conn.execute(\n        \"UPDATE task_drafts SET body = ?, updated_by = ?, updated_at = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n        (_stored(body), actor, version, draft_id),\n    )\n    return await get_draft(tx.conn, draft_id)\n\n\nasync def discard_draft(tx: Tx, draft_id: str, expected_version: str) -> None:\n    await _open_row(tx.conn, draft_id, expected_version)\n    await tx.conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM task_drafts WHERE id = ?\", (draft_id,))\n\n\n# -- publication -------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nasync def publish(\n    tx: Tx, req: PublishRequest, actor: str, *, hourly_limit: int | None = None\n) -> PublishResult:\n    \"\"\"Validate and publish a batch (3.3), idempotently by key (3.4).\"\"\"\n    digest = _digest(req)\n    async with tx.conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT request_digest, answer FROM task_draft_publications\"\n        \" WHERE idempotency_key = ?\",\n        (req.idempotency_key,),\n    ) as cur:\n        seen = await cur.fetchone()\n    if seen is not None:\n        if seen[\"request_digest\"] != digest:\n            raise ConflictError(\n                \"this idempotency_key was used for another publish request\",\n                code=\"idempotency_key_reused\",\n            )\n        answer = PublishResult.model_validate_json(seen[\"answer\"])\n        return answer.model_copy(update={\"replayed\": True})\n\n    ids = [d.draft_id for d in req.drafts]\n    rows = await _rows(tx.conn, ids)\n    outcomes: dict[str, PublishOutcome] = {}\n    bodies: dict[str, TaskDraftBody] = {}\n    outside: dict[str, str] = {}  # published drafts outside the batch -> task id\n    for item in req.drafts:\n        row = rows.get(item.draft_id)\n        if row is None:\n            outcomes[item.draft_id] = _rejected(\n                item.draft_id, \"not_found\", \"draft not found\"\n            )\n        elif row[\"published_at\"] is not None:\n            outcomes[item.draft_id] = _rejected(\n                item.draft_id,\n                \"draft_published\",\n                f\"already published as task {row['published_task_id']}\",\n            )\n        elif row[\"updated_at\"] != item.expected_version:\n            outcomes[item.draft_id] = _rejected(\n                item.draft_id,\n                \"stale_version\",\n                f\"draft changed since you read it (version {row['updated_at']})\",\n            )\n        else:\n            bodies[item.draft_id] = TaskDraftBody.model_validate_json(row[\"body\"])\n    refs = {d for b in bodies.values() for d in b.depends_on_drafts} - set(ids)\n    for ref, row in (await _rows(tx.conn, sorted(refs))).items():\n        if row[\"published_task_id\"] is not None:\n            outside[ref] = row[\"published_task_id\"]\n    for draft_id, body in bodies.items():\n        if why := _incomplete(body, outside, set(ids)):\n            outcomes[draft_id] = _rejected(draft_id, \"validation_failed\", *why)\n\n    order, cycles = _order(ids, {i: b.depends_on_drafts for i, b in bodies.items()})\n    for draft_id, path in cycles.items():\n        outcomes.setdefault(\n            draft_id,\n            _rejected(\n                draft_id,\n                \"dependency_cycle\",\n                \"these drafts depend on each other: \" + \" -> \".join(path),\n            ),\n        )\n\n    task_ids: dict[str, str] = dict(outside)\n    for draft_id in order:\n        if draft_id in outcomes:\n            continue\n        body = bodies[draft_id]\n        if waits := [d for d in body.depends_on_drafts if d not in task_ids]:\n            outcomes[draft_id] = PublishOutcome(\n                draft_id=draft_id,\n                outcome=\"skipped\",\n                errors=[f\"depends_on_drafts: {d} was not published\" for d in waits],\n            )\n            continue\n        create = TaskCreate.model_validate(\n            {\n                **body.model_dump(exclude_unset=True, exclude={\"depends_on_drafts\"}),\n                \"depends_on\": [\n                    *body.depends_on,\n                    *(task_ids[d] for d in body.depends_on_drafts),\n                ],\n            }\n        )\n        try:\n            async with tx.savepoint():\n                task = await service.create_task(\n                    tx, create, actor, hourly_limit=hourly_limit\n                )\n                await _check_capabilities(tx.conn, task.required_capabilities)\n                await tx.conn.execute(\n                    \"UPDATE task_drafts SET published_at = ?, published_task_id = ?,\"\n                    \" publication_key = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n                    (ts(tx.now), task.id, req.idempotency_key, draft_id),\n                )\n                await record(\n                    tx,\n                    actor,\n                    \"task_draft\",\n                    draft_id,\n                    \"task_draft.published\",\n                    {\"task_id\": task.id, \"idempotency_key\": req.idempotency_key},\n                )\n        except DomainError as exc:\n            outcomes[draft_id] = _rejected(\n                draft_id, exc.code, exc.message, *exc.details\n            )\n            continue\n        task_ids[draft_id] = task.id\n        outcomes[draft_id] = PublishOutcome(\n            draft_id=draft_id, outcome=\"published\", task_id=task.id, state=task.state\n        )\n\n    result = PublishResult(\n        idempotency_key=req.idempotency_key,\n        mode=req.mode,\n        items=[outcomes[i] for i in ids],\n    )\n    failed = [o for o in result.items if o.outcome != \"published\"]\n    if req.mode == \"atomic\" and failed:\n        raise _atomic_refusal(failed)  # the write transaction rolls back\n    await tx.conn.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO task_draft_publications (idempotency_key, request_digest,\"\n        \" answer, actor, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n        (req.idempotency_key, digest, result.model_dump_json(), actor, ts(tx.now)),\n    )\n    return result\n\n\ndef _incomplete(\n    body: TaskDraftBody, outside: dict[str, str], batch: set[str]\n) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Why a draft is not a complete task definition yet (3.3), or nothing.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        TaskCreate.model_validate(\n            body.model_dump(exclude_unset=True, exclude={\"depends_on_drafts\"})\n        )\n        errors = []\n    except ValidationError as exc:\n        errors = _errors(exc)\n    if not body.spec.strip():\n        errors.append(\"spec: a draft needs a spec to be published\")\n    if not body.acceptance:\n        errors.append(\"acceptance: a draft needs at least one criterion\")\n    elif any(not a.strip() for a in body.acceptance):\n        errors.append(\"acceptance: criteria cannot be blank\")\n    errors += [\n        f\"depends_on_drafts: {d} is not in this batch\"\n        for d in body.depends_on_drafts\n        if d not in batch and d not in outside\n    ]\n    return errors\n\n\ndef _order(\n    ids: list[str], edges: dict[str, list[str]]\n) -> tuple[list[str], dict[str, list[str]]]:\n    \"\"\"The batch in dependency order, and each draft on an in-batch cycle with\n    that cycle's path. Edges to drafts outside the batch are ignored here.\"\"\"\n    batch = set(ids)\n    deps = {i: [d for d in edges.get(i, []) if d in batch] for i in ids}\n    order: list[str] = []\n    done: set[str] = set()\n    while True:\n        ready = [i for i in ids if i not in done and all(d in done for d in deps[i])]\n        if not ready:\n            break\n        order += ready\n        done.update(ready)\n    cycles: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    for start in ids:\n        if start not in done and (path := _cycle_from(start, deps)):\n            cycles[start] = path\n    # Drafts left behind a cycle come last; they are skipped as not published.\n    return order + [i for i in ids if i not in done], cycles\n\n\ndef _cycle_from(start: str, deps: dict[str, list[str]]) -> list[str] | None:\n    \"\"\"A path start -> ... -> start along dependency edges, if one exists.\"\"\"\n    stack: list[tuple[str, list[str]]] = [(start, [start])]\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    while stack:\n        node, path = stack.pop()\n        for dep in deps[node]:\n            if dep == start:\n                return [*path, start]\n            if dep not in seen:\n                seen.add(dep)\n                stack.append((dep, [*path, dep]))\n    return None\n\n\nasync def _check_capabilities(conn: aiosqlite.Connection, required: list[str]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Each capability must be declared by a pool or a non-archived agent.\"\"\"\n    if not required:\n        return\n    async with conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT j.value FROM pools, json_each(pools.capabilities) AS j\"\n        \" UNION SELECT j.value FROM agents, json_each(agents.capabilities) AS j\"\n        \" WHERE agents.archived_at IS NULL\"\n    ) as cur:\n        known = {r[0] for r in await cur.fetchall()}\n    if unknown := [c for c in required if c not in known]:\n        raise ValidationFailedError(\n            \"no pool or agent declares these capabilities: \" + \", \".join(unknown),\n            code=\"unknown_capability\",\n            details=[f\"required_capabilities: {c}\" for c in unknown],\n        )\n\n\ndef _atomic_refusal(failed: list[PublishOutcome]) -> DomainError:\n    codes = [o.code for o in failed if o.code]\n    code = next((c for c in _PRECEDENCE if c in codes), codes[0] if codes else None)\n    cls = {\n        \"not_found\": NotFoundError,\n        \"stale_version\": ConflictError,\n        \"draft_published\": ConflictError,\n    }.get(code or \"\", ValidationFailedError)\n    details = [\n        f\"{o.draft_id}: {o.code or o.outcome}: {e}\" for o in failed for e in o.errors\n    ]\n    return cls(\n        f\"nothing was published: {len(failed)} draft(s) cannot be published\",\n        code=code if code in _PRECEDENCE else \"validation_failed\",\n        details=details,\n    )\n\n\ndef _rejected(draft_id: str, code: str, *errors: str) -> PublishOutcome:\n    return PublishOutcome(\n        draft_id=draft_id, outcome=\"rejected\", code=code, errors=list(errors)\n    )\n\n\ndef _digest(req: PublishRequest) -> str:\n    canonical = json.dumps(\n        {\n            \"mode\": req.mode,\n            \"drafts\": [[d.draft_id, d.expected_version] for d in req.drafts],\n        },\n        separators=(\",\", \":\"),\n    )\n    return hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\n# -- rows --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _stored(body: TaskDraftBody) -> str:\n    # Only fields the author set: a kind's defaults still apply at publish.\n    return json.dumps(body.model_dump(mode=\"json\", exclude_unset=True), sort_keys=True)\n\n\ndef _errors(exc: ValidationError) -> list[str]:\n    return [\n        f\"{'.'.join(map(str, e['loc'])) or 'body'}: {e['msg']}\" for e in exc.errors()\n    ]\n\n\nasync def _row(conn: aiosqlite.Connection, draft_id: str) -> aiosqlite.Row:\n    async with conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT * FROM task_drafts WHERE id = ?\", (draft_id,)\n    ) as cur:\n        row = await cur.fetchone()\n    if row is None:\n        raise NotFoundError(f\"draft not found: {draft_id}\")\n    return row\n\n\nasync def _rows(conn: aiosqlite.Connection, ids: list[str]) -> dict[str, aiosqlite.Row]:\n    if not ids:\n        return {}\n    marks = \",\".join(\"?\" * len(ids))\n    sql = f\"SELECT * FROM task_drafts WHERE id IN ({marks})\"  # noqa: S608\n    async with conn.execute(sql, ids) as cur:\n        return {r[\"id\"]: r for r in await cur.fetchall()}\n\n\nasync def _open_row(\n    conn: aiosqlite.Connection, draft_id: str, expected_version: str\n) -> aiosqlite.Row:\n    row = await _row(conn, draft_id)\n    if row[\"published_at\"] is not None:\n        raise ConflictError(\n            f\"draft {draft_id} was published as task {row['published_task_id']};\"\n            \" edit the task instead\",\n            code=\"draft_published\",\n            details=[row[\"published_task_id\"]],\n        )\n    if row[\"updated_at\"] != expected_version:\n        raise ConflictError(\n            f\"draft {draft_id} changed since you read it (version\"\n            f\" {row['updated_at']}); read it again and reapply your change\",\n            code=\"stale_version\",\n            details=[row[\"updated_at\"]],\n        )\n    return row\n\n\ndef _to_draft(row: aiosqlite.Row) -> TaskDraft:\n    return TaskDraft(\n        id=row[\"id\"],\n        body=TaskDraftBody.model_validate_json(row[\"body\"]),\n        version=row[\"updated_at\"],\n        created_by=row[\"created_by\"],\n        created_at=row[\"created_at\"],\n        updated_by=row[\"updated_by\"],\n        updated_at=row[\"updated_at\"],\n        published_at=row[\"published_at\"],\n        published_task_id=row[\"published_task_id\"],\n    )\n","numLines":423,"startLine":1,"totalLines":423}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015Er9YseZpFfmp3eViB2qze","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
